---@field BoundingBox? aws.geo_maps.PositionListString|distilled.Secret Takes in two pairs of coordinates in World Geodetic System (WGS 84) format: [longitude, latitude], denoting south-westerly and north-easterly edges of the image. The underlying area becomes the view of the image.
---@field BoundedPositions? aws.geo_maps.PositionListString|distilled.Secret Takes in two or more pair of coordinates in World Geodetic System (WGS 84) format: [longitude, latitude], with each coordinate separated by a comma. The API will generate an image to encompass all of the provided coordinates.
---@field Center? aws.geo_maps.PositionString|distilled.Secret Takes in a pair of coordinates in World Geodetic System (WGS 84) format: [longitude, latitude], which becomes the center point of the image. This parameter requires that either zoom or radius is set.
---@field ColorScheme? aws.geo_maps.ColorScheme|string Sets the color tone for the map, such as dark and light.
---@field CompactOverlay? aws.geo_maps.CompactOverlay|distilled.Secret Takes in a string to draw geometries on the image. The input is a comma separated format as follows format: [Lon, Lat]
---@field CropLabels? boolean It is a flag that takes in true or false. It prevents the labels that are on the edge of the image from being cut or obscured.
---@field GeoJsonOverlay? aws.geo_maps.GeoJsonOverlay|distilled.Secret Takes in a string to draw geometries on the image. The input is a valid GeoJSON collection object.
---@field Height aws.geo_maps.SensitiveInteger|distilled.Secret Specifies the height of the map image.
